  message: "Related shape seen in kotlin while doing WI-rabum-zatur-rufav-busol-lurop-gisur-zojif-gidun (not the imports-map case this item names, the same family: a local named like a TYPE). With a project `object out { fun println(x: String?) {} }` and `class Sink { fun println(...) }` in one file, `val out = Sink(); out.println(k)` emits calls -> `Main.kt:6-6:out.println:method` (the OBJECT's method), not Sink.println: kotlin.py's call arm tests `receiver_name in class_symbols` (Case 2, static/object call) before the receiver's var_types entry. A confidently-wrong call edge, not an unresolved one. Measured at the rabum branch tip on a one-file fixture; not measured on the corpus."  # c074
